case.summary:
{
  "investigation_summary": "The alert was triggered by a flagged card-not-present transaction (ID 3464869) for $599.94 from an unfamiliar device (Trident/7.0 on Windows 8.1, IE 11.0) with a risk score of 0.77. This transaction deviates sharply from the card's historical behavior (C03042-K1 averages 30 transactions at $88.22), indicating a potential compromise. The pattern matches prior confirmed fraud case CC-0615, which also involved a card-not-present new device and resulted in a $174.99 loss. Given the high fraud probability (0.90) and supporting evidence, the transaction is assessed as fraudulent."
}

sar.narrative:
{
  "narrative": "Customer C03042, card C03042-K1, exhibited a card_not_present_new_device pattern with total exposure $8,110.87 across transactions 3054463 ($49.91), 3054510 ($200.00), 3054511 ($24.97), 3054532 ($200.01), and 3063365 ($100.04). An additional flagged transaction 3464869 for $599.94 occurred online with a risk score of 0.77. Transaction 3464869 originated from device D8A3375, identified as Trident/7.0 (Windows 8.1, IE 11.0) with resolution 1680x1050. Device D8A3375 is associated with eight cards, including C03042-K1, and is marked as new for this card. Card C03042-K1 has a historical average transaction amount of $88.22 based on 30 prior transactions. The amount of transaction 3464869 ($599.94) is substantially above the card’s historical average. Prior closed cases for this card/customer include CC-0615, CC-1313, and CC-3886, with CC-0615 and CC-3886 confirmed as fraud under the same card_not_present_new_device pattern. No other cards are connected to C03042-K1."
}
